From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: HDR10 Rendering Reference

The Vulkan engine's HDR10 output can map to a display the user
describes instead of to the film's own peak (DVVK_HDR10_TARGET,
CroqueMr's CB1 "LLDV Reference - HDR10 Output"), sending that
display's static metadata, but Kodi had only the Master Reference
conversion.

Settings > Player > Dolby Vision gets HDR10 conversion: Master
Reference (the default, the conversion and signalling as before) or
Rendering Reference, with Display peak brightness (50 to 10000 nits,
1000), Display black level (CB1's OLED 0, LCD 0.005, projector 0.05,
or a custom 0 to 0.5 nits) and Display colours (P3-D65, BT.2020,
BT.709), shown only for Rendering Reference (DV_HDR10_TARGET, _PEAK,
_BLACK, _GAMUT). It applies wherever the engine's HDR10 output is
used: Convert to HDR10, the Automatic fallback to it, Convert to
HDR10+ while it is HDR10. The HDR static metadata is
dvvk_output_signal's, as before.

The settings are offered where the HDR10 output is and the library
takes DVVK_HDR10_TARGET (dvvk_target_flags), and stay shown while
Rendering Reference is saved. A library without it, values out of
range from native-dv.env, or the engine refusing the mode give the
Master Reference conversion with a log line: still an HDR10 picture.
Player information names Rendering Reference and the display.

Not yet seen on a display. With Master Reference the engine gets the
same mode as before and dvvk_target_flags is not called while playing.

Strings 45171 to 45188; Custom is 45151.
